-> T26: `loop a { }` must NOT resolve the outer `a` — visiting every
-> possibility isn't the same as picking one (agreed explicitly with the
-> owner, not a default). After the loop, `a` is exactly as unresolved as
-> before it, so using it in an operation still fails.
a ∈ { 1, 2, 3 }
loop a get doubled {
    yield a * 2
}
b = a + 1
